    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Geographic information systems (GIS) are extremely useful tools for managing and correlating large amounts of spatial data. This paper reviews some of the key concepts involved in using a geographic information system and gives examples of basic GIS capabilities. GIS technology is combined here with mapping projects to illustrate its potential utility in structural geology and rock fracture problems. Specific applications to the petroleum industry are also suggested.",
